---
import { personal, skills } from "@/data/portfolio";
import PageLayout from "@/layouts/Base.astro";

const meta = {
	title: "About",
	description:
		"Backend Software Engineer focused on .NET, C#, distributed systems, APIs, and cloud-native architecture.",
};
---

<PageLayout meta={meta}>
	<h1 class="title mb-8 text-2xl">About</h1>
	<div class="prose prose-sm prose-cactus max-w-none">
		<p>
			I'm a Backend Software Engineer based in Cairo, Egypt, working primarily with .NET and C#.
			I build scalable APIs, distributed systems, and cloud-native applications, with a focus on
			clean architecture, reliability, and observability.
		</p>
		<p>
			At Health Insights Group, I contribute to a healthcare platform built on .NET Core — working on
			backend modules, redesigning real-time notification systems with SignalR and Redis, and
			collaborating with clinical and product teams to deliver production-ready features.
		</p>
		<p>
			Before that, I worked as an intern at EJADA Systems building CRM features with C# and .NET Framework,
			and as a web security researcher on HackerOne, where I disclosed vulnerabilities for organizations
			including the U.S. Department of Defense and AT&T. That security background directly informs
			how I approach API design, authentication, and system architecture.
		</p>
		<p>
			I enjoy working on problems involving scalability, performance, distributed communication,
			authentication and authorization, observability, and system reliability. Beyond .NET, I've
			built systems in Go and Java/Spring Boot to broaden my perspective on backend engineering patterns.
		</p>
		<p>
			I'm always interested in connecting with engineers working on challenging backend systems.
			Feel free to reach out via
			<a href={`mailto:${personal.email}`} class="cactus-link">{personal.email}</a> or
			<a href={personal.linkedin} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer" class="cactus-link">LinkedIn</a>.
		</p>
	</div>
</PageLayout>
